From 6912b85cb7b902616ad786dfc20afe3b4cf28b10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@soprasteria.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 16:58:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: rate Dispel Life against living monsters like the game
 does

The Dispel Life evaluation kept damage only for monsters flagged both
NONLIVING and UNDEAD, the inverse of the game's drain, which damages
each living monster and treats undead or nonliving monsters as immune
(monster_is_nonliving).  With no NONLIVING monsters in the game data
the spell was rated at zero damage against every monster kind, so the
Borg never considered casting it.  Zero the damage for nonliving
monsters only.

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-fight-attack.c b/src/borg/borg-fight-attack.c
index 45c5d140a..3fa9f4799 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-fight-attack.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-fight-attack.c
@@ -578,11 +578,11 @@ static int borg_launch_damage_one(int i, int dam, int typ, int ammo_location)
             dam = 0;
         break;
 
-    /*  Dispel life */
+    /*  Dispel life: the game's drain only hurts living monsters
+     * (nonliving is undead or nonliving). */
     case BORG_ATTACK_DRAIN_LIFE:
-        if (!(rf_has(r_ptr->flags, RF_NONLIVING)))
-            dam = 0;
-        if (!(rf_has(r_ptr->flags, RF_UNDEAD)))
+        if (rf_has(r_ptr->flags, RF_NONLIVING)
+            || rf_has(r_ptr->flags, RF_UNDEAD))
             dam = 0;
         break;
 
